extraction_notes: "TEMPLATE CLASS: printed 126-127 calls the Whack Job Scientist the equivalent of the RCSG Field Scientist, with skills, related and secondary skills and equipment ''same as the CS RCSG Scientist'' plus additions and substitutions. The base is production''s cs-rcsg-scientist (Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.82-84), written out here in full (a same-as class ships a full copy); its MOS block and related-skill categories are copied verbatim. No copy_of is declared: nearly every top-level key differs. GROUP: the Geofront Military O.C.C.s section, Regular Army (printed 121, ''Scientist/Whack Job O.C.C. (RCSG Scientist)''), so men-of-arms as the base is; S.D.C. 4D6+15 is printed, so no men_of_arms line. XP: the Geofront Whack Job Scientist column of printed 160. I.S.P.: ''Permanent I.S.P. Base (Chi)'', M.E. x2 +1D6 per level, stored without a psionic tier; the class learns no Mystic Martial Art Power (''None''), so no more Chi comes from one. ATTRIBUTES AND BONUSES: China''s own (I.Q. 12, M.E. 10, a high P.P. helpful but not required; +2 I.Q. and +2 vs Horror Factor) replace the RCSG''s (I.Q. 10, M.E. 10; +1 vs possession and level-gated Horror Factor and magic saves). The +1 attack per melee is the bionic arms'' (Cybernetics line), stored as a combat bonus because every Whack Job starts with the arms. RCSG ABILITIES NOT CARRIED: the RCSG''s special abilities (Lore: Geomancy or Ley Lines, Ley Line Drifting, Ley Line Rejuvenation, Recognize Enchantment, Recognize Magic) are RCSG training rather than skills, and China states only the skills as ''same as''; they are not copied. A judgement - the Geofront regards magic as a matter for the supernatural (printed 127). SKILLS: the RCSG list plus China''s additions: Mathematics: Basic +20% (same as the RCSG''s), Language: Chinese at 95% and Literacy: Chinese +20% in place of American and Literacy: America, Pilot: Bicycle +20% (Bicycling), Read & Operate Sensory Equipment +20% (Sensory Equipment), Chinese Alchemy +15%, Criminal Science & Forensics +10% (stored as the catalog''s Forensics, the nearest row), Medical Doctor +15%, M.D. in Cybernetics +15% and Pathology +20%. HAND TO HAND: ''Substitute Basic Hand to Hand with Tai-Chi (that''s it)'': Tai-Chi is granted and costs is empty. MYSTIC MARTIAL ART POWER: printed None. EQUIPMENT: China''s armor line (Shadow Armor, M.D.C. dress uniform, Standard Brigandine) replaces the RCSG''s light Dead Boy armor and its dress uniform; its weapons line (one handgun and one rifle of choice, which may be Chi weapons or experimental items, four clips each) replaces the RCSG''s energy rifle, sidearm and E-Clips; the choices are the Geofront and Chi guns in the catalog and the clips are 8 ammunition-clips. The rest of the RCSG kit is ''basically the same'' and copied. CYBERNETICS: China''s list replaces the RCSG''s (''ignore those''); it is prose under Whack Job Cybernetics, and the five implants with gear rows (gyro-compass, clock calendar, security clearance chip, headjack, finger camera) are also equipment. No rows exist for the tentacle bionic arms, a cybernetic language translator, amplified hearing or sound filtration (bio-wizard versions only), a sensor hand matching ''Sensor Hand'', the multi-optic eye, the cyber-camera, or the molecular analyzer and oxygen cell lung implants; no stubs were made. MONEY: the RCSG prints 1D4x1000 credits to start; half is 1D4x500. No racial line is printed; none is stored."
---

## Lore

The Geofront''s Whack Job Scientists are its combat scientists, the
counterpart of the Coalition''s Rift Control Study Group. They prize
knowledge, progress and the success of whatever project is in front of them
above nearly everything, human life included; their allegiance to the
Geofront is the one thing they put ahead of it. They are as fierce as any soldier about freeing
China, and fascinated by demon physiology and magic.

The ones who leave their laboratories go to see the outside world, to learn,
to watch their inventions - demon-skin armor, Chi weapons and the rest - in
action, and to study the enemy up close so it can be destroyed more
efficiently. Centuries ago, people of their temperament became China''s
alchemists and would-be Immortals. Almost all of them have rebuilt their own bodies with bionics,
most visibly a pair of tentacle-like mechanical arms.

## GM Notes

Most have good intentions, but unprincipled, anarchist, aberrant and even
miscreant scientists are common. Use the CS RCSG Scientist as the template for
anything the book does not change.
